@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<div class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
</div>
<div class="panel" style="max-width: 42rem;">

<p>McWut is for the people who were invited. It is not a public site. This page is only here once you are signed in.</p>

<h2 class="h5">What we keep</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Your email, the name you choose, the color you pick, and a hash of your sign-in password.</li>
    <li>Files you save, including the name, type, and size. A file stays until you delete it, unless you choose a number of days.</li>
    <li>Notes you paste, saved as text files.</li>
    <li>A share link only when you make one. A password on the file is asked for when someone opens that link. You can still open the file while signed in.</li>
    <li>Short links, and the web address they open.</li>
    <li>Logins in your vault. The name is plain text. The username, password, address, and notes are encrypted. Only you can open that list.</li>
    <li>A short record of uploads, downloads, and deletes.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="h5">Who can see a file</h2>
<ul>
    <li>You, while you are signed in.</li>
    <li>Someone who has a share link you made, until you delete the link or the file expires.</li>
    <li>Someone who opens a short link is sent to the address you saved. They do not see your files.</li>
</ul>
<p>Photos can be looked at. A note, including Markdown, can be read on My files and on a share page when the link allows it. That open is not counted as a download. SVG and HTML stay downloads.</p>

<h2 class="h5">Your name and color</h2>
<p>The name and color live on your profile. They are for the family, later, so we can tell each other apart. They are not put on a public link.</p>

<p>An admin can turn an account off, or set a new sign-in password. Turning an account off does not delete the files. Delete a file while you are signed in to remove it. To close an account, ask the person who invited you.</p>

<p class="mb-0">Do not save anything you are not allowed to keep.</p>
</div>
